"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs and Bank of America disclose that their capital positions and planning are subject to the risk of higher-than-expected capital requirements due to evolving regulatory capital rules. GS specifically highlights the risk that actual capital requirements may be higher than anticipated due to changes in U.S. bank regulatory capital rules. Similarly, BAC states that its evolving regulatory capital rules influence planning processes and may require additional regulatory capital, noting that these rules are complex and continue to evolve.",
