"comparison": "Goldman Sachs and JPMorgan Chase both identify U.S. regulatory capital rule revisions as a key factor influencing their capital requirements. GS warns that actual capital requirements may be higher due to revisions to U.S. bank regulatory capital rules. JPM details that the Federal Reserve and OCC establish requirements consistent with Basel III and notes that U.S. banking regulators released a proposal in July 2023 to amend the U.S. risk-based capital framework to incorporate elements of the revised international Basel III capital framework.",
