"comparison": "Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley both address the impact of proposed comprehensive revisions to U.S. capital requirements based on Basel III standards. GS notes that its capital ratio targets are subject to risk from changes in regulations, including revisions to U.S. bank regulatory capital rules. Morgan Stanley explicitly states that the U.S. banking agencies have proposed a comprehensive set of revisions to their capital requirements based on changes to the Basel III capital standards finalized by the Basel Committee.",
